  "definition": "Trajectory planning is the process of computing a time-parametrised path \u2014 specifying position, velocity, and acceleration profiles \u2014 that moves a robot from a start configuration to a goal while satisfying kinematic and dynamic constraints, joint limits, and task requirements. It extends path planning by assigning timing to waypoints, enabling smooth, jerk-limited motions suitable for real-time execution by a robot controller.",
